WEBVTT

00:07:59.202 --> 00:08:01.885
My name is Andrew Marantz,
I write for "The New Yorker,"

00:08:01.909 --> 00:08:04.430
my personality type
is like if a Seinfeld episode

00:08:04.454 --> 00:08:06.291
was taped at the Park Slope Food Coop.

00:08:06.315 --> 00:08:07.477
Nothing?

00:08:07.501 --> 00:08:10.014
(Laughter)

00:08:12.804 --> 00:08:15.035
Anyway, look -- ultimately,
it would be nice

00:08:15.059 --> 00:08:17.407
if there were, like, a simple formula:

00:08:17.431 --> 00:08:21.419
smartphone plus alienated kid
equals 12 percent chance of Nazi.

00:08:21.918 --> 00:08:23.522
It's obviously not that simple.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.353
And in my writing,

00:08:25.377 --> 00:08:28.592
I'm much more comfortable
being descriptive, not prescriptive.

00:08:29.049 --> 00:08:31.690
But this is TED,